## Complete Basic xCAT Setup for *Head Node*

With xCAT installed, register the internal provisioning interface with xCAT for
DHCP service. Then set the cluster domain name used for system-wide name
resolution.

<!-- ohpc_begin -->
<!-- ohpc_comment Complete basic xCAT setup for head node -->
```bash
# Verify required variables are set
: "${sms_eth_internal:?ERROR: sms_eth_internal not set}"
: "${sms_ip:?ERROR: sms_ip not set}"

# Register internal provisioning interface with xCAT for DHCP
chdef -t site dhcpinterfaces="xcatmn|${sms_eth_internal}"

# Point provisioning services at the internal interface address. Without
# this, a multi-homed head node may auto-select its external address.
chdef -t site master=${sms_ip} nameservers=${sms_ip}

# Define local domain name
chdef -t site domain=${dns_domain:-local}
```
<!-- ohpc_end -->
